(first opening the balcony door)

Balcony
A wide balcony, looking out over the sleeping city. Below you, a lawn slopes gently away into the gloom, a few silhouetted trees marking the edge of the modest grounds. Above, the clear sky is a deep black, dusted with glinting stars.

To the south-east is a large, tinted glass window.

To the south, the door to the upstairs corridor lies open.

>wait until 4:20:25
Time passes.

>smash window
You swing the crowbar firmly into the window and it shatters with a loud crash.

A piercing siren rings out.

>enter window

Conference Room
A rather slick but soulless affair. A large table of dark polished wood takes pride of place and is surrounded by a half-dozen chairs.

To the north, lie the shattered remains of a window, open to the starry night.

On the conference table is a collection of notes.

The siren wails.

>take notes
Taken.

The siren wails.

>exit

